; Not steps after the first: a rule that takes.  Under step every over a set
; store, make-c reads (a) at every state, and its match, whose row was there a
; step before, still counts: take-c takes the (c) it made, and make-c makes it
; again in the same step.  Meeting only the matches that read a fresh row would
; lose (c), so this program's steps meet every match.
(store set)
(step every)
(a)
(rule make-c (read (a)) (make (c)))
(rule take-c (take (c)) (make (d)))
